82b35dcf381ccf236f62556158019f1f7baf9b8.001.1"},{"event":"Flash Flood Warning","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued September 16 at 9:45PM MDT until September 17 at 12:45AM MDT by NWS Grand Junction CO","description":"FFWGJT\n\nThe National Weather Service in Grand Junction has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nNorth Central Mesa County in west central Colorado...\n\n* Until 1245 AM MDT.\n\n* At 945 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 0.4 and 0.7 inches of\nrain have fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 2 to 4 inches in 1\nhour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin shortly.\n\nHAZARD...Life threatening flash flooding. Thunderstorms producing\nflash flooding.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Life threatening flash flooding of creeks and streams,\nurban areas, highways, streets and underpasses.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nCameo.","ends":"2026-09-17T00:45:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Mesa, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d2f2ca415de238570bc493abab04dc4da94431e.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.7d2f2ca415de238570bc493abab04dc4da94431e.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-17T04:50:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 170450 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 1050 PM MDT Wed Sep 16 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Flash flooding will be possible for the coming days as record moisture propagates through eastern Utah and western Colorado. - Flood Watches remain in effect for SE Utah and SW Colorado today through Thursday. - Impacts from flash flooding could observed ","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-09-16T18:50:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Sub-tropical moisture continues to propagate through the area which is feeding shower and thundersto